    "text": "By Kalyn ,\n18 hours ago Centennial is often overshadowed by its neighbours — Denver with its culinary swagger, Greenwood Village with its corporate polish, and Aurora with its global‑flavour density. But locals know a different Centennial: a food city shaped by Korean and Vietnamese families, Mexican traditions, old‑school diners, and small, independent kitchens that thrive in modest spaces rather than chase RiNo‑style trendiness. Read full article",
